# Title:  Credential dumping - LSASS access
# MITRE:  T1003.001 - OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory
# Data:   Sysmon EventCode 10 (ProcessAccess)
# Why:    LSASS holds credential material in memory. Anything opening a high-privilege
#         handle to it is either a security product or someone dumping credentials. Also
#         catches dbghelp.dll / dbgcore.dll in the call stack, the debug libraries most
#         credential dumpers rely on to write a minidump.
# Noise:  Effectively none, and that is by design -- see below.
#
# Tuning: DO NOT add a GrantedAccess filter here. sysmon-modular already restricts
#         collection against lsass to credential-dumping-grade masks inside the Sysmon
#         config itself, so the filtering happens before the event is ever written.
#         Filtering again in SPL adds nothing and only risks suppressing a real hit.
#
#         Case note: the config XML writes these masks uppercase (0x1F1FFF) but they
#         arrive in Splunk lowercase (0x1f1fff). Splunk field-value comparisons are
#         case-sensitive, so anyone copying masks straight out of the config into SPL
#         will get a filter that silently matches nothing. Another reason not to.
#
#         Verified 2026-08-26: 1658 ProcessAccess events in 24h, zero against lsass.exe.
#         The credential-dumping masks (0x1fffff, 0x1410, 0x1010) DO appear in the data,
#         but against Docker/Chrome/Discord via the `contains Desktop` include rule --
#         not against lsass. Mask presence alone means nothing without the target.
#         That is the expected state for a clean machine, not a broken detection. The
#         high-volume TargetImage values (Docker Desktop, Chrome, Discord) come from an
#         unrelated `TargetImage contains Desktop` include rule and are excluded here.

index=endpoint source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=10
    (TargetImage="*lsass.exe" OR CallTrace="*dbghelp.dll*" OR CallTrace="*dbgcore.dll*")
| table _time, host, SourceImage, TargetImage, GrantedAccess, CallTrace
| sort - _time
